#!r6rs ; -*- scheme -*-
(import (akku format manifest))

;; The package installs the libraries under src/. Akku installs any library
;; it finds, so .akkuignore lists the directories outside src/ that hold
;; one, bench, build, grammar, site, tests and vendor, and, as circuit's
;; does, .claude, .plans, .superpowers and AGENTS.md. `make check-akku` installs the
;; package as a consumer would, and checks that exactly src/'s libraries land
;; (ADR-0003, ADR-0022).
;;
;; depends: the generated parser imports (byte-machine runtime). The range's
;; floor is the version vendored in vendor/byte-machine, which the suites run
;; against, and Akku.lock locks the same version. `make check-versions`, which
;; `make test` runs, holds the three together. `make check-pins`, on the host,
;; also holds vendor/byte-machine's gitlink at its pin (ADR-0002).
;;
;; depends/dev: chez-cmark-gfm renders docs/ into the docs site (`make site`,
;; ADR-0021). Nothing under src/ and no tests/test-*.sps imports it.
;;
;; The version follows semantic versioning: before 1.0, any release may
;; change the API, and a new minor version comes with a new byte-machine
;; runtime ABI or a move to a new byte-machine 0.x, such as from ^0.8.0 to
;; ^0.9.0. CHANGELOG.md's newest release and the home page's Status name the
;; same version; `make check-release` holds the three together (ADR-0022).
(akku-package ("jsonparse" "0.2.0")
  (synopsis "A fast, strict JSON parser for R6RS Scheme, generated by byte-machine")
  (description
   "A resumable JSON parser: feed it bytes as they arrive, split anywhere. It is strict RFC 8259, reports byte offsets, and builds trees or calls back with events."
   "Its libraries need only (rnrs) and byte-machine's runtime.")
  (authors "Kiyomi Computation Systems LLC")
  (homepage "https://github.com/Kiyomi-Computation-Systems/jsonparse")
  (license "BSD-3-Clause")
  (depends ("byte-machine" "^0.9.0"))
  (depends/dev ("chez-cmark-gfm" "^2.0.0")))
